silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_05_sections_01_concrete_anchor_6#erroneoussupersededtypenode silm:hasLongDescription "The ErroneousSupersededTypeNode is the re-typing target for the historical-trace. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'erroneous_superseded', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
